SYNTHESIS
  PROVED: half-tiling size H_n=floor((n-1)^2/4)=(F_n+fixed_n)/2.
  PROVED: even and odd half-tilings obey different exact recurrences.
  BRIDGE: full A+B+C-D-E-F+G is third difference; half-tiling is its
          mirror-folded parity refinement.
  WARNING: these are cell-count recurrences. OCF/Hamiltonian-path counts
           are cycle-space invariants and need packet/root data.
